# Bot2 owns the District Mascot (cast on turn 2 with a Llanowar Elves). Turn 4: it attacks unsaddled and gets no counter (Bot1 at 19), and with
# one counter the destroy ability is refused although mana and an artifact target (Bot1's Mox Pearl) are there. Turn 6: saddled by the Elves it
# attacks, grows to 2/2 and, after combat, removing its two counters destroys Bot1's Mox Pearl: Bot1 loses its own artifact to Bot2's ability.
# (Bot1, doing nothing, discards an Island to hand size on turn 5, so it sits under the Mox Pearl in its graveyard.)

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Island x19

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
District Mascot
Llanowar Elves
Forest
Forest
Forest
Forest x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Hand.District Mascot.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Attack(District Mascot > Bot1)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T4 Bot2.Main2]
? Bot1.Life = 19
? Bot2.Battlefield.District Mascot.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
! Bot2.Battlefield.District Mascot.Activate(Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl; Ability: Destroy)
[T6 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.District Mascot.Activate(Ability: Saddle)
Bot2.Choose(Llanowar Elves)
Bot2.Attack(District Mascot > Bot1)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Bot2.Battlefield.District Mascot.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 2
[T6 Bot2.Main2]
? Bot1.Life = 17
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest#1.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest#2.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.District Mascot.Activate(Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl; Ability: Destroy)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl = (absent)
Bot1.Graveyard = Mox Pearl; Island
Bot2.Graveyard = District Mascot
